## 1. What Is Coding-Decoding?

In coding-decoding questions, a word, number, letter, symbol, or sentence is transformed into another form according to a hidden rule.

Your task is to:

```text
INPUT
  ↓
Find hidden rule
  ↓
Apply rule
  ↓
OUTPUT
```

Example:

```text
CAT → DBU
```

Observe:

```text
C → D  (+1)
A → B  (+1)
T → U  (+1)
```

Therefore:

```text
DOG → EPH
```

because:

```text
D → E
O → P
G → H
```

---

## 2. The Core Idea

Every coding question has three parts:

```text
┌──────────────┐
│ ORIGINAL     │
│ INFORMATION  │
└──────┬───────┘
       ↓
┌──────────────┐
│ HIDDEN       │
│ TRANSFORM    │
└──────┬───────┘
       ↓
┌──────────────┐
│ CODED        │
│ INFORMATION  │
└──────────────┘
```

The most important skill is **not calculation**.

It is:

> Finding the transformation rule.

---

## 3. Major Types of Coding-Decoding

| Type | Main idea |
|---|---|
| Letter coding | Letters are shifted/rearranged |
| Number coding | Letters/words become numbers |
| Word coding | Whole words are replaced |
| Substitution coding | Object is represented by another word |
| Sentence coding | Words are represented by symbols/codes |
| Chinese coding | Common words reveal common codes |
| Mixed coding | Letters + numbers + symbols |
| Matrix coding | Code positions correspond to a grid |
| Conditional coding | Rule changes according to conditions |
| Position coding | Alphabet positions are manipulated |
| Reverse coding | Alphabet/order is reversed |
| Symbol coding | Symbols represent operations/letters |
| Binary-style coding | Characters mapped to 0/1 patterns |
| Pattern coding | Visual or structural pattern is encoded |

---

